From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:14:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: Treat Kalambo as Mahua for QSEECOM and the PD
 mapper

Kalambo, the 6-core Snapdragon X2 Plus X2P-42-100, is Mahua without CPU
cluster 0, and its laptops' trees name only "qcom,kalambo" at their
root. The in-kernel protection domain mapper and the QSEECOM allowlist
match on "qcom,mahua", so on Kalambo the audio and sensor DSP services
never find their domains, and the UEFI variables stay out of reach.

Give Kalambo Mahua's entries in both tables: Glymur's ADSP and CDSP
domains, and QSEECOM as on the other Snapdragon X2 parts.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c  | 1 +
 drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_pd_mapper.c | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index 184874c..a41a0be 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2315,6 +2315,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "ecs,liva-qc710" },
 	{ .compatible = "lenovo,yoga-c630", .data = &qcom_qseecom_ro_uefi, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,glymur", },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,kalambo", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,mahua", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sc8180x", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sc8280xp", },
diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_pd_mapper.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_pd_mapper.c
index 64ca99d..3fe5f0b 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_pd_mapper.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_pd_mapper.c
@@ -625,6 +625,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_pdm_domains[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,glymur", .data = glymur_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,hawi", .data = kaanapali_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,kaanapali", .data = kaanapali_domains, },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,kalambo", .data = glymur_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,mahua", .data = glymur_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,milos", .data = sm8550_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,msm8226", .data = NULL, },
